 "researcher_notes": "Match check: no existing GEM row covers Freer to Sinton. P0258 Tejas Gas Pipeline is the old network (Refugio to Fort Bend); P0373 Corpus Christi Pipeline is Sinton to Corpus Christi, a different line. Not the same project as the EIA Kinder Morgan Texas Pipeline Expansion Project (EIA Historical Projects row 1099: 30 mi, 30 in, 500 MMcf/d, Kimmeridge-supported, Webb County; also the Webb County Extension row 1119). The EIA Aug 2026 release, Historical Projects sheet, row 1094, lists this line as Eagle Ford Project: Kinder Morgan Tejas Pipeline, new pipeline, completed Nov 2023, 67 mi, 42 in, 2000 MMcf/d, 251 million USD, intrastate, Freer to Sinton TX. A Kinder Morgan press release from July 2023, with Pipeline and Gas Journal and Oil and Gas Journal coverage, states about 67 miles of 42-inch pipe from the KMTP compressor station near Freer to the Tejas system near Sinton, about 251 million USD, planned for the fourth quarter of 2023. Press sources trace to one Kinder Morgan release; EIA is a separate compiler but cites the same release. Length is about 108 km, above the 25 km threshold. The 2 Bcf/d figure in the press release is for the combined Tejas and Dos Caminos projects; EIA assigns 2000 to this row, so capacity is medium confidence. The 62 mile 36 inch Dos Caminos line (Webb County to Freer, EIA row 1095) is a separate project, not staged here. Status operating rests on the EIA completion date only; no operator in-service notice was found. Intrastate, so no FERC filing expected; Texas Railroad Commission T-4 not checked. No official GIS route found; route not researched. Tier medium (single origin for press; EIA corroborates)."
